<div style="width:640px; box-sizing:border-box; padding:36px 34px 32px; background:#f8f6f2;">
  <p class="lbl" style="color:#b07a3c; margin-bottom:8px;">Case three · the failure that taught me the most</p>
  <p class="disp" style="font-size:26px; margin-bottom:8px;">Nothing was broken. The prompt had grown six times.</p>
  <p style="font-size:14px; line-height:1.65; color:#6b6057; margin:0 0 28px;">Quality started degrading around the fourth session per user. Context had simply accumulated until the model was drowning in its own history.</p>

  <div style="display:flex; gap:12px;">
    <div style="width:44px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; justify-content:space-between; height:270px; padding-bottom:2px;">
      <p class="num cap" style="font-size:11px; color:#b5a08a;">36k</p>
      <p class="num cap" style="font-size:11px; color:#b5a08a;">18k</p>
      <p class="num cap" style="font-size:11px; color:#b5a08a;">0</p>
    </div>
    <div style="flex-grow:1;">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 520 270" width="520" height="270" style="display:block;" aria-label="System prompt characters growing from session one to session four">
        <line x1="0" y1="1" x2="520" y2="1" stroke="#e8e2da" stroke-width="1"></line>
        <line x1="0" y1="135" x2="520" y2="135" stroke="#e8e2da" stroke-width="1"></line>
        <line x1="0" y1="269" x2="520" y2="269" stroke="#d8cec0" stroke-width="1"></line>

        <polygon points="120,228 400,24 400,269 120,269" fill="#efe9e1"></polygon>
        <rect x="40" y="228" width="80" height="41" fill="#c9bfb2"></rect>
        <rect x="400" y="14" width="80" height="255" fill="#1e1a16"></rect>

        <line x1="0" y1="209" x2="520" y2="209" stroke="#b07a3c" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 5"></line>
        <text x="516" y="203" text-anchor="end" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="11" font-weight="600" fill="#b07a3c">BOUNDED PROMPT: HARD BUDGET</text>

        <text x="80" y="218" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="600" fill="#1e1a16">5,600</text>
        <text x="440" y="6" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="600" fill="#1e1a16">34,000+</text>
        <text x="260" y="130" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#8a7d6e">accumulated, session on session</text>
      </svg>
      <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr)); margin-top:8px;">
        <p class="lbl" style="color:#8a7d6e; text-align:center;">Session 1</p>
        <p class="lbl" style="color:#b5a08a; text-align:center;">2</p>
        <p class="lbl" style="color:#b5a08a; text-align:center;">3</p>
        <p class="lbl" style="color:#8a7d6e; text-align:center;">Session 4</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p style="font-size:13px; line-height:1.6; color:#8a7d6e; margin:22px 0 0; padding-top:16px; border-top:1px solid #e8e2da;">Sessions two and three are shown as accumulation rather than measured points. The two figures are the ones I recorded.</p>

  <div style="margin-top:18px; display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:flex-start;">
    <div style="width:9px; height:9px; border:1.5px solid #b07a3c; border-radius:50%; flex-shrink:0; margin-top:5px; background:#b07a3c;"></div>
    <p style="font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; color:#1e1a16; margin:0;">The fix was architectural, not cosmetic: hard character budgets, enforced regardless of how many sessions a user has had.</p>
  </div>
</div>
